    "Confirmed wiring preserved: LM35 on A1 as analog_input, fan PWM on D5 as pwm_output, and overheat LED on D13 as digital_output. No other circuit pins were provided, so no additional requests were added.",
    "Serial baud and framing preserved: baud=9600 and framing=line_or_idle with idle_timeout_ms=20.",
    "Repaired serial_command_input mapping: io_3.commands now maps 1..32 to printable ASCII tokens (each token is mapped to a unique i32 code). Exact semantics of each token (how it adjusts/sets temperature threshold and minimum fan speed) are intentionally left to the SysML/model layer.",
    "LM35 conversion to degC and fan PWM scaling/minimum-speed behavior are handled in the SysML model; scale/offset for analog_input and pwm_output are left as 1/0 placeholders because no explicit calibration parameters were provided.",
    "Control period set to 10 ms as previously proposed scheduling granularity."
